                 === AETHERMUD STAFF NEWS ===

Read this once. Most of it is here because somebody already lost a boot
to it.

RELOADING: UPDATE IS NOT ENOUGH FOR /std/
  update <path>   recompiles one file's blueprint. Safe and sufficient
                  for anything under /daemon/, /cmds/, and single room
                  files. _update.c moves players to the void and back
                  around a room reload, so updating the room you are
                  standing in is fine.
  warmboot        same limitation, wider blast radius.
  full reboot     ./mud.sh stop && ./mud.sh start, from the shell.

  In LPC, inherit is resolved at compile time. Anything that already
  inherited /std/room.c, /std/user.c, /std/living.c, /std/armour.c,
  /std/monster.c, /std/container.c and so on keeps running the OLD code
  after you update the parent. Every loaded room, every connected
  player, every spawned NPC. If you touched a file under /std/ or under
  secure/cmds/, only a full reboot actually ships it. Never tell anyone
  warmboot covers those.

  Never use kill on the driver. Always mud.sh.

COMPILING ON FLUFFOS 2.9
  Declare every variable at the TOP of its function, before any
  statement. C89 rules, strictly. Mixed declarations and code will not
  compile.
  Use /* */ comments. Not //.
  A function must be declared before it is called. Calling something
  defined further down the same file is a compile error, so add a
  prototype near the top. See the prototype blocks in daemon/rifts.c,
  setter.c, std/monster.c.
  When an object mysteriously fails to load, the error is in
  log/errors/<dir>, NOT log/runtime. This is where a missing prototype
  hides. /std/monster once failed for an entire boot this way and no
  NPCs loaded anywhere.

BUILDING ROOMS
  Spawn NPCs and objects in reset(), never in create(). Guard each one
  with present("id", this_object()). Cloning in create() breaks
  update <path> and can duplicate or crash. Patterns to copy:
  domains/Praxis/square.c, domains/Praxis/hospital.c.
  Never describe a spawned NPC or object in set_long(). They are real
  objects and list themselves below the exits line; naming them in the
  long text makes them appear twice, in the wrong order.
  Room display order is description, exits, NPCs, objects. Already
  correct in std/user.c describe_current_room(). Do not reorder it.
  set_smell() and set_listen() text appears only when a player types
  smell or listen. Never put it in set_long().
  Do not add ambient messages. The mixin was removed on purpose; they
  interrupted players.

APIS THAT DO NOT EXIST
  Containers use set_max_encumbrance(n). There is no set_max_weight().
  NPC Mega-Damage uses set_stats("MDC", n) and set_stats("max_MDC", n).
  There is no set_mdc() on monsters, only on rifts_vehicle.c.
  Non-combat damage goes through
  RIFTS_COMBAT_D->apply_direct_damage(victim, damage). Do not call
  do_damage() with a named limb.

THE DAMAGE MODEL
  Damage is pooled on one pseudo-limb called whole_body. Per-limb
  damage and limb targeting are retired. Order of depletion is
  protective spell fields, then worn armor pools, then MDC or SDC and
  hit points. Limb severing still exists but is narrative only, via the
  admin sever command. Do not rename whole_body; it is serialized into
  player saves.

PATHS
  Player saves      /secure/save/users/<first letter>/<name>.o
                    NOT /save/players/. That path is dead.
  Wiz tools         /domains/adm/wiz_tools/
  Board saves       /secure/save/boards/
  Daemons must be listed in secure/cfg/preload.cfg or they will not
  exist at boot.
  log_file() prepends /log/ itself, so pass a path relative to it:
  log_file("adm/setrole", ...). write_file() takes the literal absolute
  path. Mixing the two produces /log//log/ paths.

WRITING TEXT
  American spelling in player-facing strings: armor, color, defense.
  The FILE /std/armour.c and its function names stay British. Do not
  rename them.
  No em dashes anywhere, in strings, help files, or comments. Use a
  hyphen, comma, or colon.
  Multi-word ability names collapse for help keys: help armorofithan,
  help remoteviewing. Never show underscores to a player.

COMMUNICATION RULES
  This game has NO player chat channels. All player-to-player reach is
  room-local, except telepathy (needs an introduction, costs ISP) and
  radio (needs a carried, tuned radio item). tell and reply are staff
  contact only.
  Before you add a player command: if it loops users(), or uses
  find_player() or tell_object() to reach somebody who is not present()
  in the room, that is a bug. This applies to system notifications too,
  not just open chat.

THE STAFF BOARD
  A shared bulletin board now stands in the Wizard's Lounge, the Admin
  Chamber, and admin workrooms. All copies share one thread pool, so a
  note posted at one shows up at all of them. post <subject>,
  read <number>, followup <number>, remove <number>.
  Looking at it also prints live pending queues: accounts awaiting
  approval, skill requests, and apprentice submissions, with the
  command to act on each. Check it when you log in.

TESTING SOMETHING TRICKY
  Metamorph and disguises: query_apparent_race() deliberately returns
  the TRUE race to the character themselves, to any creator, and to
  anyone who already knows them. A staff character can never see their
  own disguise work, and a staff disguise is inert for everyone. Test
  it on a mortal, observed by a different mortal.
